#!/bin/sh
# Runs automatically on every `git push`. No memory required.
# Bypass in a genuine emergency with: git push --no-verify

set -e

printf '\n\033[1m→ lint\033[0m\n'
npm run lint

printf '\n\033[1m→ typecheck + build\033[0m\n'
npm run build

printf '\n\033[1m→ tests\033[0m\n'
npm test

cat <<'REMINDER'

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The machine checked what it can. It cannot check these:

  · Every statement in STATEMENTS.md, clicked through
  · Loading / empty / error states actually render
  · Blast radius — who else imports what you changed
  · Core paths still work

Fried and unsure? Do not push. Verify in the morning.
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

REMINDER
